    "reason": "The assertion claims a specific application is defined by having a narrow task scope. This is factually unsound because many specific applications (e.g., general-purpose coding assistants, multi-modal analysis tools) have broad or evolving scopes yet remain 'specific' to their domain context. Narrow scope is not a necessary condition for defining a specific application.",
    "sound_as_stated": false,
    "counterexample": "A general-purpose code generation tool used by developers across various languages and frameworks has a broad task scope but is still a specific application within the software development domain."
  },
  "candidate_0068": {
    "reason": "The assertion claims narrow task scope applications do not utilize broad general knowledge encoded in foundation models. This is false; even narrow applications often leverage foundation models trained on vast datasets to perform their specific tasks effectively (e.g., a medical diagnosis tool using an LLM trained on all medical literature). The utilization of broad knowledge does not preclude a '","sound_as_stated": false,
    "counterexample": "A specialized legal document summarizer built on a foundation model utilizes the model's broad general knowledge to identify relevant statutes and precedents, despite its narrow task scope."
  },
  "candidate_0069": {
    "reason": "The assertion states that broad general knowledge encoded in foundation models is represented by parameters encoding such knowledge. This is well-established: the weights (parameters) of a neural network are the mathematical representation of the information and patterns learned during training, including broad general knowledge.",
    "sound_as_stated": true,
    "counterexample": null
  },
  "candidate_0070": {
    "reason": "The assertion claims broad general knowledge is irrelevant to specific applications. This is false; the breadth of knowledge often enables robustness and adaptability in specific applications (e.g., handling out-of-distribution inputs). While relevance varies, stating it is universally 'irrelevant' ignores cases where general knowledge directly aids specific performance.",
    "sound_as_stated": false,
    "counterexample": "A customer service chatbot using a foundation model relies on its broad general knowledge to understand diverse user queries and empathetic responses, which are crucial for its specific application."
  }
}
